Package: claude-usage
Version: 0.11.28
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-cairo, python3-pil, systemd
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 45) | plasma-desktop, google-chrome-stable | chromium-browser
Description: Claude.ai usage indicator for GNOME and KDE Plasma
 Shows Claude.ai weekly usage percentage in the GNOME or KDE Plasma panel
 and dock.
 .
 Features a two-ring dock icon (All models outer ring, Sonnet only inner
 ring), a color-coded panel label with scroll-wheel toggle between metrics,
 and user-configurable ring colors via the native preferences UI on either
 desktop (GNOME extension prefs or KDE plasmoid config).
 .
 Data is fetched every 7 minutes by the Claude Usage Tracker Chrome
 extension, which reads your existing Claude.ai session — no API keys or
 stored credentials required.
 .
 After installing this package, run: claude-usage-setup
